{
  "_comment": "virp-onode-home device template (node_id 0x0000000D, 10.0.0.13). TRACKED 2026-09-03. Until then this node's fleet existed ONLY as /etc/virp/devices.json on the box: no template, no render step, no unit-manifest row, 38 devices and four plaintext credentials that no commit described. A rebuild would have lost the whole fleet silently. That is the same failure the colo node had with its 43 devices, one node over. Rendered to /run/virp/devices.json at daemon start by deploy/render-devices.sh, substituting ${...} from /etc/virp/autopilot.env (0600 root). This template carries NO credentials.",
  "_credentials_required": "autopilot.env on this node must define exactly four values, and render-devices.sh is FATAL on any placeholder it cannot resolve \u2014 the daemon refuses to start rather than authenticate as a literal ${TOKEN}. VIRP_PVE_PASSWORD (pve-lab root), VIRP_LABNET_PASSWORD (aiops-svc, shared by all 35 GNS3 routers), VIRP_WAZUH_HOME_PASSWORD (virp-ro on wazuh-home), VIRP_FORTIGATE_HOME_PASSWORD (virp-gate on fortigate-home). Confirmed by hashing every credential in the live config and its eleven backups on 2026-09-03: four distinct values, no more. NOTE the 35 routers share ONE credential \u2014 compromise of any one of them is compromise of all thirty-five, which is a property of the lab, recorded here rather than fixed here.",
  "_socket_allowlist_policy": "uid 0 is EXCLUDED, same as the colo node: a client running as root is rejected at the peercred gate. 999 is the daemon's own service account, 1000 the interactive operator, 997 virp-spark (the Spark's requester identity), 1001 virp-laptop (the laptop approver identity, reaching the socket over a forwarded stream).",
  "socket_allowed_uids": [
    "${VIRP_UID}",
    1000,
    997,
    1001
  ],
  "socket_uid_tier_ceilings": {
    "${VIRP_UID}": "green",
    "1000": "green",
    "997": "green",
    "1001": "green"
  },
  "_socket_uid_action_allow_note": "FIXES A LIVE DEPLOY BLOCKER (found 2026-09-02, Phase 0). Until this file, only 997 and 1001 had action maps. 999 and 1000 were allowlisted with NO entry, and the daemon treats an allowed-but-unmapped uid as UNRESTRICTED \u2014 `shutdown` included. Since the Sep 1 review (Task 2) onode_start() REFUSES TO RUN when this object does not cover the allowlist, naming the uid. So on the binary this node runs today the gap is a silent grant, and on origin/main it is a boot failure: upgrading this node without this row would not have started. Adding 999 and 1000 here is a NARROWING, not a grant \u2014 999 loses `shutdown` it implicitly held, and both gain an explicit ceiling where they had none.",
  "socket_uid_action_allow": {
    "${VIRP_UID}": [
      "execute",
      "health",
      "heartbeat",
      "list_devices",
      "list_fleet",
      "sign_intent",
      "sign_outcome",
      "chain_append",
      "chain_verify",
      "chain_verify_session",
      "intent_store",
      "intent_get",
      "intent_execute",
      "batch_execute",
      "validate_turn",
      "approval_challenge",
      "approval_submit",
      "session_hello",
      "session_bind",
      "session_close"
    ],
    "1000": [
      "execute",
      "health",
      "heartbeat",
      "list_devices",
      "list_fleet",
      "sign_intent",
      "sign_outcome",
      "chain_append",
      "chain_verify",
      "chain_verify_session",
      "intent_store",
      "intent_get",
      "intent_execute",
      "batch_execute",
      "validate_turn",
      "approval_challenge",
      "approval_submit",
      "session_hello",
      "session_bind",
      "session_close",
      "shutdown"
    ],
    "997": [
      "execute",
      "list_fleet",
      "health",
      "chain_verify"
    ],
    "1001": [
      "approval_challenge",
      "approval_submit",
      "list_fleet",
      "execute",
      "health"
    ]
  },
  "_socket_uid_chain_append_types_note": "Second half of the same blocker: absent entirely on this node until now. A uid whose action set includes chain_append MUST appear here or the daemon refuses to start naming it. Only 999 and 1000 may chain_append; 997 and 1001 have no chain_append verb and correctly have no entry. `evidence_item` is present so the deployed-state reporter can land its document as a real body rather than a commitment-only hash every reader would grade UNVERIFIABLE \u2014 see the matching note in deploy/devices.template.json. Types use the 16-byte-truncated spellings the wire delivers.",
  "socket_uid_chain_append_types": {
    "${VIRP_UID}": [
      "observation",
      "comparator_verd",
      "chainwalk_summa",
      "evidence_item"
    ],
    "1000": [
      "observation",
      "comparator_verd",
      "chainwalk_summa",
      "evidence_item"
    ]
  },
  "_gate_posture_note": "gate_max_tier is GREEN here, tighter than the colo node's YELLOW, and deliberately unchanged by this file. pve-lab has NO Proxmox classifier, so its commands land RED-by-absence and are proposal-only and fail-closed. Tracking a config is not the moment to change what it permits: this template is byte-for-byte the posture the node was already running, plus the two policy objects whose ABSENCE was the bug.",
  "gate_default_mode": "enforce",
  "gate_max_tier": "green",
